---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { appStoreBadge, appsBySlug, companionApps } from "../../data/site";

const app = appsBySlug.glasshole;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Glasshole AI"
  description="Glasshole AI is an iPhone app for AI-powered live fact-checking and overlay for spoken conversation."
  path="/apps/glasshole"
>
  <article class="container prose">
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="page-header__brand">
        {
          app.icon && (
            <img
              class="page-header__icon"
              src={app.icon}
              width="72"
              height="72"
              alt={app.iconAlt || "Glasshole AI"}
            />
          )
        }
        <div>
          <p class="page-header__kicker">iPhone · App Store</p>
          <h1 class="page-header__title">Glasshole AI</h1>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="page-header__lead">
        Glasshole AI is an iPhone app with optional wearable companion support.
        It also works standalone on iPhone.
      </p>
      {
        app.appStoreUrl && (
          <p class="page-header__actions">
            <a
              class="store-badge-link"
              href={app.appStoreUrl}
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              aria-label={`Glasshole AI — ${appStoreBadge.alt}`}
            >
              <img
                src={appStoreBadge.src}
                width={appStoreBadge.width}
                height={appStoreBadge.height}
                alt={appStoreBadge.alt}
              />
            </a>
          </p>
        )
      }
    </header>

    <p>
      The app acts as an AI-powered live or real-time fact-checker and overlay
      for spoken conversation. It can transcribe spoken conversation, summarize
      it, and surface concise factual analysis on iPhone and on the companion
      display.
    </p>

    <h2>Supported Modes and Models</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Apple Intelligence on compatible iPhones</li>
      <li>xAI Grok</li>
      <li>OpenAI</li>
      <li>Anthropic Claude</li>
      <li>Google Gemini</li>
      <li>Ollama</li>
      <li>PocketPal</li>
      <li>Custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Consent and Recording</h2>
    <p>
      Glasshole records audio only when a user starts a session. Use it only with
      the consent of everyone being recorded and in compliance with local laws
      and regulations where it is used.
    </p>
    <p>
      Audio recordings are not saved. On-device speech recognition converts audio
      to text, and session history is stored locally on device. If the user
      selects an external AI provider, only the transcript needed for the request
      is sent to that provider.
    </p>

    <h2>Optional Wearable Companion (Google Glass XE)</h2>
    <p>
      The optional Google Glass XE companion lets you start sessions from Glass
      and view returned results on the prism. The companion connects to the
      iPhone app over local Wi-Fi or iPhone Personal Hotspot.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Requires:</strong> Google Glass XE, ADB on a computer, and an
      iPhone Personal Hotspot. Connect Glass to the iPhone hotspot before
      opening Glasshole AI.
    </p>

    <h3>Install path: this page → GitHub</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Download the companion APK from the button below (or from the
        <a
          href="https://github.com/scalinghuman/experiments/releases/tag/glass-companions-v1.0.0"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub release</a
        >).
      </li>
      <li>
        Follow the
        <a href={companionApps.glasshole.guideUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Google Glass XE installation guide on GitHub</a
        >
        for ADB install, USB debugging, and hotspot setup.
      </li>
      <li>Open this iPhone app and confirm the connection indicator.</li>
      <li>
        On Glass, open the <strong>fact check</strong> command and
        <strong>tap</strong> the touchpad to launch — then tap again to
        start/stop listening.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      <strong>Do not rely on saying “Ok Glass.”</strong> Use the touchpad tap
      on the <strong>fact check</strong> Glass command.
    </p>
    <p class="page-header__actions">
      <a class="btn btn--secondary" href={companionApps.glasshole.apkUrl}>
        Download Google Glass companion (APK)
      </a>
      <a href={companionApps.glasshole.guideUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Installation guide on GitHub
      </a>
    </p>

    <h2>Notes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>AI-generated summaries and fact-check results can be wrong.</li>
      <li>
        Results should be treated as assistive output, not authoritative truth.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="links-row">
      <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>
      <a href="/support.html">Support</a>
      <a href="/">Home</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
